+
+2026-10-08 inventory correction: Python 3.10 `-S` does not reliably set the
+virtual-environment prefix. The inventory binds `pyvenv.cfg` beside/above the
+invoked executable without resolving its executable symlink first. It records
+virtual-environment and base-interpreter search paths and selected dependency
+records separately, including cross-scope duplicates. Only explicitly enabled
+system site packages enter the active dependency set; ambiguous active records
+block admission. No `.pth`, site customization or scientific package is executed.
+This is standard installed-metadata evidence, not proof of runtime import paths.
+
+The inventory hashes actual METADATA bytes for dist-info and actual PKG-INFO
+bytes for standard egg-info, including their exact paths. Missing, empty or
+malformed metadata in any discovered descriptor rejects the inventory; there is
+no empty-string digest fallback. Errors and valid records remain visible in
+stdout with exit code 2. Active duplicates are not silently overwritten. The
+test entry retains invalid metadata in its blocked report before package imports.
+The 13 added invented-record regressions bring the expected unittest inventory
+to 143; they do not constitute Linux or full-suite acceptance. Historical
+130-case evidence and its old source lock remain unchanged in the prior package.
 
